From: =?UTF-8?q?Tor=20Arne=20Vestb=C3=B8?= <tor.arne.vestbo@qt.io>
Date: Mon, 10 Jan 2022 16:51:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] eglfs: Unset shared raster compositing context before
 deletion

Backport to 5.15: without this, every top-level window created after the
first one has been destroyed is set to share with a QOpenGLContext that
QEglFSWindow::destroy() has already deleted (qt_gl_global_share_context()
is never cleared). On vt-sbc-am62l the SignaSteam first-boot flow -
orientation dialog, then setup wizard, then MainWindow, each a separate
top-level window - hits that dangling pointer in
QEglFSIntegration::createPlatformOpenGLContext (shareHandle() on freed
memory) and dies with SIGSEGV the moment the wizard's Finish button is
pressed. Whether the freed block has been reused by then decides between a
crash and a silent read of stale memory, which is why it only showed on
landscape units.

Upstream-Status: Backport [Qt 6, f3db9abebf7e1ea6bb929b05cb62cb7052414be0]
Signed-off-by: Eric Tanner <eric.tanner@harvia.com>

Change-Id: Ib0f615c76ac62f1177e44faaa733e67014f4185d
Reviewed-by: Laszlo Agocs <laszlo.agocs@qt.io>
---
 src/plugins/platforms/eglfs/api/qeglfswindow.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/plugins/platforms/eglfs/api/qeglfswindow.cpp b/src/plugins/platforms/eglfs/api/qeglfswindow.cpp
index 9cd1f17f5fb..47f6d88e5cc 100644
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/eglfs/api/qeglfswindow.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/eglfs/api/qeglfswindow.cpp
@@ -177,6 +177,8 @@ void QEglFSWindow::destroy()
 
 #ifndef QT_NO_OPENGL
         QOpenGLCompositor::destroy();
+        if (qt_gl_global_share_context() == m_rasterCompositingContext)
+            qt_gl_set_global_share_context(nullptr);
         delete m_rasterCompositingContext;
 #endif
     }
